 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? The manual gives the right height, but it' usually a bit too high. The correct height for you is when you can ride comfortably with your feet flat on the pedals. Try it at height where your feet just touch the bottom. That's probably too low, so add a few spacers and try again. Got it. Add spacers, then test again. Stop when you can still reach the floor with a flat foot. That's good. It means you' not reaching, so you' less likely to strain them. Mostly. The seat is taller than the handlebars, so your body leans forward. Most people can reach the ground with a hand on the ground.",
